From ac47589b1103d2a67546e832f92fb09d02f6c09c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77ph <tk@itarragon.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:56:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(operator): hardware-signed Kernel owner for the
 service Safe (agent-signer)

Optional config section signer: { kind: 'agent-signer', bin, config,
account, envFile?, sponsored? }. With it, the venue's Safe transactions are
sent by a TPM_sign Kernel account (ERC-4337) that owns the Safe: one
UserOperation per Safe transaction, signed by an agent key inside a TPM /
Secure Enclave / TROPIC01 through the agent-signer CLI, and judged on-chain
by the account's AgentPolicy (inner call allow-list, value caps, no Safe
self-administration).

- src/signer/agent-signer-cli.ts: the CLI as a typed call, failure kinds
- src/signer/kernel-safe-broadcaster.ts: BaseVenueSafeBroadcaster on top of
  execTransaction(v = 1); Safe nonce asserted on-chain; attempts written
  ahead to the venue ledger and reconciled by userOpHash, never re-executed
- src/signer/agent-signer-transport.ts: viem transport for direct calls;
  off-chain signing refused
- boot refuses when signer.account is not an owner of the service Safe

Without the section nothing changes. Scope: the venue loop (claim, deliver,
settle, verdict, posting); off-chain signatures, direct EOA writes and
bootstrap still use the keystore agent EOA.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
